From ac323d76fe562392fca883ffd29cbc65d6863f33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LumenForge Fix <fix@lumenforge.dev>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 18:39:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Multi-mask rework: real per-mask storage, target-aware paint
 tools, crop/export fixes

- DocumentModel: replace setActiveMask()/activeMask() (always wrote/read
  m_masks[0]) with addMask()/removeMask()/maskImage()/setMaskImage(), so
  masks are independently created, painted, and deleted by id.
- DocumentController: brush/gradient/radial/AI-subject-mask/refine-edges/
  inpaint all read and write the mask matching activeAdjustmentTarget
  instead of always mask index 0. ensurePaintTarget() auto-creates a mask
  the first time a paint tool is used with Full Image selected.
  syncBrushEngineToTarget() reloads the paint surface whenever the
  selected mask changes, so strokes never land on stale content left by
  the previously-selected mask.
- addNewMaskTarget() now calls the real DocumentModel::addMask() instead
  of only faking an adjustment-target id with no backing mask image.
- clearMask() now removes the mask entry and every Adjustment targeting
  it (DocumentModel::removeMask), instead of nulling mask[0]'s pixels and
  leaving an orphaned entry + orphaned adjustments behind. QML buttons
  relabelled Clear -> Delete to match.
- applyCrop() crops every mask's pixel data by the identical rect, so
  masked regions stay aligned to content instead of drifting to absolute
  canvas coordinates after a crop.
- Per-mask temp preview files: m_maskTempPath (single) -> m_maskTempPaths
  (per mask id), so maskUrl()/maskList() show the correct mask regardless
  of which one is selected.
- RenderPipeline::renderFullResolution() now delegates to the same
  renderWithLayers() path the on-screen preview already uses correctly
  (adjustmentsForTarget("") for globals + per-mask loop), instead of
  adjustmentsForLayer("") which returned every adjustment including
  mask-scoped ones and double-applied them. This also adds overlay-layer
  compositing to the export path, which it never had before.
